            "text": "Under $25, name-brand everyday carry is the sweet spot. The Victorinox Swiss Army Classic SD, the Milwaukee Fastback utility knife and the Black Diamond Astro 300 headlamp are all products enthusiasts actually carry, and they are used weekly. If you are buying for a man you do not know well, a small pocket knife or headlamp is a very safe choice."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What are good stocking stuffers for men?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "The best stocking stuffers for men are consumables and small, single-job tools. Duke Cannon soap, O'Keeffe's Working Hands hand cream, a ThermoPro instant-read thermometer, a magnetic stud finder and a chainsaw file kit all work well, and most come in under $20. They are useful from day one and either get used up or fix a problem he has been putting off."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Is it rude to give an inexpensive Christmas gift?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "No. A cheap gift feels cheap only when it looks random. An inexpensive Christmas gift for a man that matches how he actually spends his time, comes with a one-line note about why you chose it and is the best version of its kind reads as thoughtful. Plenty of men prefer a $20 tool they use every week to an expensive gadget they never touch."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What can I buy for a man at the last minute?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Many picks here are carried by mainstream stores. Lodge cast iron, Milwaukee and Klein hand tools, Mechanix gloves, Apple AirTags, Anker chargers, O'Keeffe's and Duke Cannon are widely stocked at big-box, hardware and electronics stores. Check local inventory online before driving. If something will not arrive in time, print a photo of it and put that in the card."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What cheap gifts for men should I avoid?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Skip credit-card multi-tools, no-name electronics, hundred-piece bargain tool kits, gift sets in plastic trays and whiskey stones. These items tend to look good in the package and disappoint in use. The common thread is that their main selling point is presentation. Spending the same money on one well-made item from a known brand is almost always the better gift."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What do I get a man who already has everything?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "When he already owns the obvious things, focus on upgrades to items he uses daily, like better socks, a better utility knife or a better coffee maker, or on consumables he will not buy himself. For more ideas built for exactly this situation, see our guide to Christmas gifts for men who have everything, which goes beyond the under-$50 budget."
          }
        }
      ],
    },
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: title,
      author: authorSchema(Astro.url.pathname),
      datePublished: dates.published,
      dateModified: dates.modified,
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "The Honest Reviewers" },
    },
    {
      "@type": "ItemList",
      name: title,
      numberOfItems: PRODUCTS.length,
      itemListElement: PRODUCTS.map((product, index) => ({
        "@type": "ListItem",
        position: index + 1,
        name: product.name,
        url: new URL(`#${product.id}`, Astro.url).toString(),
      })),
    },
    ...PRODUCTS.map((product) => ({
      "@type": "Product",
      name: product.name,
      description: product.description,
      brand: {
        "@type": "Brand",
        name: product.name.split(" ")[0],
      },
    })),
  ],
};
